**Issue**: #433
**Status**: Approved
**Date**: 2026-09-24
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Reverify a repaired implementation without replaying failed evidence
  As an operator of an issue-owned execute controller
  I want a bounded exact-head recheck after a verified source repair
  So that stale failed verification neither blocks delivery forever nor bypasses gates

  @regression
  Scenario: Exact changed-head repair enables a fresh registered gate
    Given a Fail report and matching canonical gate artifact belong to head A under the active verify owner
    And a clean issue-owned repair publishes distinct head B on the same Approved spec and branch
    When the verify worker resumes under that owner
    Then the A report and artifact are archived with exact digests
    And a one-use A-to-B recheck is consumed before the registered gate runs at B

  @regression
  Scenario: Passing evidence advances only from the new head
    Given the changed-head recheck produces complete passing required validations at B
    When acceptance review approves the repaired implementation and normal finalization publishes the report
    Then the report and passed verify handoff bind B
    And the controller may advance to delivery

  @regression
  Scenario Outline: Unproved or consumed recovery does not dispatch
    Given the prior report is Fail or Partial
    And <condition> prevents exact changed-head proof
    When verify recovery is requested
    Then it does not run a new gate or overwrite report evidence
    And it leaves controller and handoff authority unchanged

    Examples:
      | condition                         |
      | the head is unchanged             |
      | the working tree is dirty         |
      | the verify owner is foreign       |
      | the report is a symlink           |
      | the spec identity changed         |
      | the recheck is already consumed   |

  @regression
  Scenario: A new failed gate guides a distinct next repair without granting delivery
    Given a valid changed-head recheck consumes its A-to-B authority
    When the registered gate at B fails and acceptance review records the changed head and remaining failure
    Then historical A evidence stays archived and a truthful B Fail report is published
    And the controller checkpoints that failure and proposes a different repair based on prior attempts
    But no passed handoff or delivery dispatch is created

  @regression
  Scenario: Progressful verify repairs are not stopped after two attempts
    Given two completed verify remediations produced distinct published source changes and new failure evidence
    When a third materially different repair is needed for the same Approved spec
    Then the controller retains all attempt evidence and may continue without a fixed total-attempt limit
    And repeated unchanged evidence or an already consumed A-to-B pair still stops

  @regression
  Scenario: Mixed local failure carries immutable feedback without accepting external incompleteness
    Given a verification report at B is Incomplete because a required command failed and external evidence is incomplete
    When the controller rewinds implementation after preserving the B report and gate artifact
    Then a distinct published C may authorize a registered recheck of the local repair
    But the incomplete external result cannot authorize a passed handoff or delivery

  @regression
  Scenario: A passing artifact cannot omit or downgrade a registered required result
    Given the active controller has a manifest with two required validations
    When a passing artifact omits one result or marks its failure optional
    Then finalization refuses the report without publishing it or passing verification

  @regression
  Scenario: Standalone Pass still requires a current registered gate
    Given a standalone verification report says Pass without a canonical gate artifact
    When the finalizer evaluates publication
    Then it refuses a passed handoff and does not publish the report

  @regression
  Scenario: Prior same-head external-only incomplete recovery remains independent
    Given an external-only Incomplete artifact remains at its original head
    When its existing one-use prerequisite recheck is requested
    Then its current exact-head and external-only gates remain unchanged

  @regression
  Scenario Outline: Distinct evidence can advance any remediable stage
    Given the controller has checkpointed two failed <stage> attempts with their exact evidence
    And the next LLM worker inspects the spec, prior failures and attempted repairs
    When it publishes a distinct <proof> under the same issue owner and normal stage gate
    Then the controller may authorize another <stage> attempt without a fixed total count
    And the worker must explain why its next approach differs

    Examples:
      | stage     | proof                         |
      | implement | synchronized source commit    |
      | review1   | newly verified review result  |
      | fix2      | synchronized source commit    |
      | verify    | exact-head registered gate    |
      | deliver   | exact-head PR check evidence  |

  @regression
  Scenario: The same stage evidence cannot authorize another dispatch
    Given a stopped remediation has no new issue-owned head, artifact or gate result
    When the controller considers another attempt
    Then it retains the checkpoint and consumed side effects unchanged
    And it reports the precise no-progress blocker
